    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d40">

                <pb facs="0061" n="49" sameAs="frus:frus1945v05/pg49"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">857.48/4–245</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Secretaries of the State-War-Navy
                        Coordinating Committee</hi><anchor n="51" xml:id="d40-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">SWNCC 24/6</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-04-07">7 April 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center">
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Relief Shipments to Enemy-Occupied Territory</hi>
                </p>
                <p>The enclosure, a draft of a letter to the Secretary of State from the Secretaries
                    of War and the Navy, as proposed by the Joint Chiefs of Staff, is circulated for
                    consideration by the Committee.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles</hi> W. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >McCarthy</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Alvin</hi> F. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Richardson</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Raymond</hi> E. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Cox</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d40-a1.xml" xpointer="d40-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d40-f1" n="51" type="source" xml:id="d40-f1-content">
                <p>According to document SWNCC 24/7, dated 12 April 1945, the State-War-Navy
                    Coordinating Committee by informal action on April 10 approved SWNCC 24/6 and
                    the letter contained in the enclosure was forwarded to the Secretary of State on
                    April 11.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
